From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucas gelfond <lucasgelfond@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/29] aout: accept sample rates down to 1 kHz

Streams below 4 kHz were refused outright, although the decoders handle
them and the output resamples to whatever the device runs at: Chromium's
3 kHz WAV and Firefox's 1 kHz Vorbis test files opened, decoded and were
never heard. Accept rates down to 1 kHz.
---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audio_output/dec.c b/src/audio_output/dec.c
--- a/src/audio_output/dec.c
+++ b/src/audio_output/dec.c
@@ -357,7 +357,8 @@ vlc_aout_stream * vlc_aout_stream_New(audio_output_t *p_aout,
                  p_format->i_rate );
         return NULL;
     }
-    if( p_format->i_rate < 4000 )
+    /* Test signals and old telephony go well below 4 kHz; resamplers cope */
+    if( p_format->i_rate < 1000 )
     {
         msg_Err( p_aout, "too low audio sample frequency (%u)",
                  p_format->i_rate );
-- 
